{# The layout of the pages of the bundle, overridden by the application to give them their look
   (architecture §5.2, §6): the same document and the same blocks as the layout of the bundle, one
   stylesheet built from assets/styles/app.css (Tailwind and DaisyUI), no script. The pages of the
   bundle come with it untouched: what they render is styled by its structure and its data-* codes.

   Two shapes, because the pages are of two kinds. A page of an interaction asks one thing of whoever is
   in front of it, a login, a consent, a code typed from an appliance, and nothing else is on it: a box in
   the middle of the screen is what that is. A page of the account is a page someone reads and comes back
   to, holding a list, a table, a heading and the way back: it takes the width of a column of text, at the
   top of the screen, and carries "account" on its main so the stylesheet can say what a panel looks like
   there. Which one a request is, is its route (architecture §5.4). #}
{% set account = (app.request.attributes.get('_route') ?? '') starts with 'heidi_interaction_account' %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% block title %}{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/app.css') }}">
    {% block head %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="{{ account ? 'min-h-dvh bg-base-200' : 'min-h-dvh bg-base-200 grid place-items-center p-4' }}">
    {% block body %}
        <main
            {% if account %}data-page="account"{% endif %}
            class="{{ account ? 'mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-col gap-5 px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14' : 'card card-body w-full max-w-md bg-base-100 shadow-xl' }}"
        >
            <h1 class="{{ account ? 'text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl' : 'card-title text-2xl' }}">{% block heading %}{{ block('title') }}{% endblock %}</h1>
            {% block content %}{% endblock %}
        </main>
    {% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
